\begin{enumerate}
\item For each machine, circle DFA or NFA to indicate which type of machine it is.
(Circle both if the machine is both and NFA and a DFA.
Circle neither if it is neither.)

\begin{center}
$M_1$:  \ DFA  \ \ \ NFA   \hspace*{1in} $M_2$:  \ DFA  \ \ \ NFA
\end{center}

\item
Complete the following table.
\begin{center}
  \large
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
  \hline
  $x$ & $x \in A$? (Y or N) & $x \in B$? (Y or N)
  \\
  \hline\hline
  100 & & \\[3mm] \hline
  110 & & \\[3mm] \hline
  011 & & \\[3mm] \hline
  1100 & & \\[3mm] \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\item
Create a new NFA for the language $A \cup B$ using a
\underline{general method} that works for
the union of any two languages.

\vfill
\vfill

